# Functions permitted to set caller-visible state.
#
# Every entry must print NOTHING, so there is never a reason to call it inside `$( )`.
# test/purity.sh enforces both halves: nothing else may mutate state, and none of
# these may write to stdout.
#
# function            why it must set rather than return
integrity_check       populates the bundle hash, scan and pin state that banner.sh and every cmd/ module read; returning eight values through stdout would be worse
parse_args            its entire job is turning flags into variables
main                  sets the routing locals and DRY_RUN before dispatch

# memo <function>   caches its own result; no other function reads the variable, so a
#                   subshell costs a recomputation and never a wrong answer.
memo zone_name        avoids a jq process per call for a value that cannot change during one invocation
